## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1 — Utility Deduplication (Zero Risk)
**1 new file, removes 4 duplicate definitions. Nothing else changes.**

#### [NEW] `modules/utils.js`
Single source of truth for shared pure utilities currently duplicated across 4 files.
Exposes on `window` so all existing callers work unchanged.

Functions to consolidate:
- `escapeHtml(str)` — currently in `file-utils.js`, `main-app.js`, `ui-modules.js`, `upload-helpers.js`
- `formatSize(bytes)` — currently in `app-init.js`, `projection-layer.js`
- `cleanFolderPath(path)` — currently in `app-init.js`, `projection-layer.js`
- `formatSpeed(bps)` — currently in `file-utils.js`, `upload-helpers.js`

Each duplicate becomes: `window.escapeHtml = window.escapeHtml || localDef` — so if `utils.js` loads first, all others skip re-defining it. **No callers need to change.**

Load order: added to `base.html` first, before all other app scripts.

---

### Phase 2 — Preview Modal Module (Medium Risk, High Value)
**`openFilePreview` is 142 lines spread across 3 different locations in `app-init.js` (L767, L2535, L2869). Plus it references `closePreviewModal`, `openFilePreviewTarget` — all tangled together.**

#### [NEW] `modules/preview-modal.js`
Extract everything related to the preview modal into one clean file:
- `window.openFilePreview(filename)` — L2535–L2676
- `window.closePreviewModal()` — L2512
- `window.openFilePreviewTarget()` — L2679
- Preview modal right-click context menu setup — L2810–L2890
- All keyboard shortcut handlers for the modal (`Escape`, arrow nav)

`app-init.js` retains only the call sites (`window.openFilePreview(name)`) — the definitions move out.

---

### Phase 3 — Context Menu Module (Medium Risk)
**`openRowMenu` is 97 lines (L1504–L1600) inside `app-init.js`. Defined twice (L1504 + L4231). It builds a full dynamic context menu with 10+ action items.**

#### [MODIFY] `modules/dialog-manager.js` → or [NEW] `modules/context-menu.js`
Extract:
- `window.openRowMenu(event, filename)` — builds and positions context menu
- `window.closeContextMenu()` — teardown
- Click-outside-to-close listener setup
- All `data-action` dispatch logic currently in the menu

`app-init.js` call sites remain unchanged.

---

### Phase 4 — QR & Connect Module (Low Risk, Self-Contained)
**404 lines in `app-init.js` (L2406–L2810) handle QR code generation, LAN/mDNS tab switching, sidebar QR rendering, and the Connect modal. This is completely self-contained.**

#### [NEW] `modules/connect-panel.js`
Extract:
- `window.renderSidebarQR()`
- `window.showConnectionInfo()`
- QR LAN/mDNS tab toggle handlers
- `window.copyQRUrl()`, `window.copyStreamUrl()`

Zero coupling to file list rendering. Safe cut.

---

### Phase 5 — Upload Tray Consolidation (Low Risk)
**`renderUploadTray` (387 lines, L3729–L4115) exists inline in `app-init.js` AND `modules/upload-tray-renderer.js` (228 lines) already exists as a separate module.**

The current architecture calls the inline `app-init.js` version. The `modules/upload-tray-renderer.js` appears to be an older/parallel version.

#### [MODIFY] `app-init.js`
Verify which version is live. If the inline 387-line version is the live one, move it into `modules/upload-tray-renderer.js` (replacing the old version) and have `app-init.js` call `window.UploadTrayRenderer.render()`.

**This is the highest-value extraction** — 387 lines out of `app-init.js`.

---

### Phase 6 — Quick Access / Recents (Very Low Risk)
**`renderQuickAccess` is 97 lines (L4154–L4250), self-contained, only called from `init()`.**

#### [NEW] `modules/quick-access.js`
Extract `renderQuickAccess()` + its data fetch + rendering helpers.
Expose as `window.renderQuickAccess()`. One call site in `init()` remains.

